    "['encapsulation source-address [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing srv6', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nsegment-routing srv6\\n encapsulation source-address 5::5\\n##\\n\\nFor Cisco devices, the equivalent command to set the SRv6 encapsulation source address would be under the `segment-routing srv6` configuration mode, specifying the same IPv6 address (5::5) as the source. \\n\\nNote: Cisco's implementation may vary slightly in syntax and context, but this is the direct functional equivalent for setting the SRv6 encapsulation source address.\", 'trans_template': 'segment-routing srv6'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'encapsulation source-address 5::5', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nsegment-routing srv6\\n encapsulation source-address 5::5\\n##\\n\\nFor Cisco devices, the equivalent command to set the SRv6 encapsulation source address would be under the `segment-routing srv6` configuration mode, specifying the same IPv6 address (5::5) as the source. \\n\\nNote: Cisco's implementation may vary slightly in syntax and context, but this is the direct functional equivalent for setting the SRv6 encapsulation source address.\", 'trans_template': 'encapsulation source-address 5::5'}]]": 1,
    "['locator [parameter1] ipv6-prefix [parameter2] [parameter3] static [parameter4]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing locator as1', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei Segment Routing IPv6 locator configuration:\\n\\n##\\nsegment-routing locator as1\\n prefix 2001:db8:15::/64 static 32\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `locator` command defines an SRv6 locator with name \"as1\" and prefix\\n- In Cisco, this is broken into two commands:\\n  1. `segment-routing locator` to create the locator\\n  2. `prefix` to specify the address and parameters\\n- The parameters remain the same: IPv6 prefix/len (2001:db8:15::/64) and static block size (32)\\n- The Cisco syntax doesn\\'t include the \"ipv6-prefix\" keyword that Huawei uses', 'trans_template': 'segment-routing locator as1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'prefix 2001:db8:15::/64 static 32', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei Segment Routing IPv6 locator configuration:\\n\\n##\\nsegment-routing locator as1\\n prefix 2001:db8:15::/64 static 32\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `locator` command defines an SRv6 locator with name \"as1\" and prefix\\n- In Cisco, this is broken into two commands:\\n  1. `segment-routing locator` to create the locator\\n  2. `prefix` to specify the address and parameters\\n- The parameters remain the same: IPv6 prefix/len (2001:db8:15::/64) and static block size (32)\\n- The Cisco syntax doesn\\'t include the \"ipv6-prefix\" keyword that Huawei uses', 'trans_template': 'prefix 2001:db8:15::/64 static 32'}]]": 1,
    "['opcode [parameter1] end', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing prefix-sid index 1 explicit-null', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]', 'segment-routing locator as1'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nsegment-routing prefix-sid index 1 explicit-null\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `opcode ::1 end` command assigns a static SID (Segment Identifier) with value `::1` and marks it as an \"end\" SID (which is equivalent to a prefix SID in Cisco terminology).\\n- The Cisco equivalent uses `segment-routing prefix-sid index` where:\\n  - `index 1` corresponds to the Huawei SID value `::1`\\n  - `explicit-null` is added because Huawei\\'s \"end\" SID implies the same behavior as Cisco\\'s explicit-null (preserving the SR header for OAM purposes)\\n- In Cisco, index values are typically used instead of full SID values for prefix SIDs, and the index maps to the same value when combined with the router\\'s prefix.', 'trans_template': 'segment-routing prefix-sid index 1 explicit-null'}]]": 1,
    "['opcode [parameter1] end-dt4 vpn-instance [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing local-block 2001:db8:15::/64', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]', 'segment-routing locator as1'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nsegment-routing local-block 2001:db8:15::/64\\nsegment-routing prefix-sid-map 2001:db8:15::100/128 vrf vpna end-dt4\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The Huawei `locator as1` defines the SRv6 local SID block which is equivalent to Cisco's `segment-routing local-block`\\n2. The `opcode ::100 end-dt4 vpn-instance vpna` maps to Cisco's prefix-SID mapping with:\\n   - `2001:db8:15::100/128` (derived from Huawei's locator prefix + opcode)\\n   - `vrf vpna` instead of Huawei's `vpn-instance`\\n   - `end-dt4` function remains the same (End.DT4 for IPv4 VPN decapsulation)\", 'trans_template': 'segment-routing local-block 2001:db8:15::/64'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing prefix-sid-map 2001:db8:15::100/128 vrf vpna end-dt4', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]', 'segment-routing locator as1'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nsegment-routing local-block 2001:db8:15::/64\\nsegment-routing prefix-sid-map 2001:db8:15::100/128 vrf vpna end-dt4\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The Huawei `locator as1` defines the SRv6 local SID block which is equivalent to Cisco's `segment-routing local-block`\\n2. The `opcode ::100 end-dt4 vpn-instance vpna` maps to Cisco's prefix-SID mapping with:\\n   - `2001:db8:15::100/128` (derived from Huawei's locator prefix + opcode)\\n   - `vrf vpna` instead of Huawei's `vpn-instance`\\n   - `end-dt4` function remains the same (End.DT4 for IPv4 VPN decapsulation)\", 'trans_template': 'segment-routing prefix-sid-map 2001:db8:15::100/128 vrf vpna end-dt4'}]]": 1,
